---
export const prerender = true
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import config from '../lib/site.mjs'

const updated = 'September 13, 2026'

const jsonld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Copyright and takedown policy',
  url: `${config.siteUrl}/dmca`,
  description:
    `How to send a copyright takedown notice to ${config.name}, and what the site does and does not host.`,
  dateModified: '2026-09-13',
}
---

<Base
  title={`Copyright and DMCA takedown policy — ${config.name}`}
  description={`${config.name} hosts no chapters and no episodes, and links only to official platforms. This page explains how a rights holder can request removal of a cover image or description.`}
  canonical="/dmca"
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section__head">
        <h1>Copyright and takedowns</h1>
        <p>We host nothing. If something here still needs to come down, here is how.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="prose__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

        <h2>What this site hosts</h2>
        <p>
          {config.name} is a catalog. It stores titles, release dates, genres, short
          synopses, scores, character profiles and thumbnail cover art, all supplied by the
          public <a href="https://anilist.co" rel="noopener">AniList</a> API.
        </p>
        <p class="prose__note">
          There are no chapters, no scans, no episodes and no video on this site. Every
          reading or streaming link points at a publisher, a licensor or a licensed
          streaming service. We do not link to scan sites, aggregators or mirrors, and we
          refuse requests to add them.
        </p>

        <h2>Cover art and synopses</h2>
        <p>
          Cover images are shown small, beside factual information about the work they
          identify, and each one points the reader towards a legal place to buy or read it.
          We believe this is fair use. If you hold the rights and disagree, we will remove
          the material rather than argue about it.
        </p>

        <h2>How to send a notice</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a class="mailto" href={`mailto:${config.dmcaEmail}`}>{config.dmcaEmail}</a>.
          Under the Digital Millennium Copyright Act, 17 U.S.C. section 512(c)(3), a valid
          notice must include all of the following:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
          <li>Identification of the copyrighted work you say is infringed.</li>
          <li>The exact page address on {config.host} where the material appears.</li>
          <li>Your name, postal address, telephone number and email address.</li>
          <li>
            A statement that you believe in good faith that the use is not authorised by
            the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.
          </li>
          <li>
            A statement that the information in the notice is accurate, and, under penalty
            of perjury, that you are the owner or are authorised to act for the owner.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2>What happens next</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We acknowledge every complete notice within 3 business days.</li>
          <li>Valid notices are actioned within 10 business days, usually much sooner.</li>
          <li>
            Because the site rebuilds from AniList every night, we also add the item to a
            permanent exclusion list so it does not come back on the next build.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Counter-notice</h2>
        <p>
          If your material was removed by mistake, send a counter-notice to the same
          address with your signature, the material removed and where it was, your contact
          details, and a statement under penalty of perjury that the removal was a mistake
          or a misidentification.
        </p>

        <h2>Repeat infringers</h2>
        <p>
          This site has no user accounts and accepts no uploads, so there is nothing for a
          third party to post here. Any platform we link to that turns out to be unlicensed
          is removed from the index permanently.
        </p>

        <h2>Wrong address?</h2>
        <p>
          If your complaint is about a scan site, we are not it, and we do not link to it.
          Please send your notice to the host of that site instead.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
